red by south african scientists  and data suggests they transfer much  faster than others people that were just  infected with omicron ba1 that was the  original one they can easily get  reinfected with ba-4 and ba-5 so we know  that this previous immunity from  previous infection  it is not very protective from second  infection but we still expect that this  immunity will be protective  against hospitalization and death  as long as hospitals remain relatively  empty virologists say there is no need  for bars to remain empty too that's why  they are not calling for tighter covet  regulations in south africa  south africa was one of the few african  countries to pay social assistance to  people who were unemployed and had no  other source of income during the  pandemic  the amount was small roughly 20 euros a  month which sparked controversy  but it helped many survive and a few to  even start a new business  event photography that's what tandoo  makubu did before the pandemics truck  but after almost all events were  cancelled he had to find new subjects to  photograph he saved about 40 euros from  his covet grants to come up with  creative ice cream designs the pictures  posted on his social media channels went  viral and he decided to open an ice  cream parlor at his mother's house  there is no idea this is a stupid idea  you know we just have to try it out and  and and work hard at it so  it feels crazy and interesting and  it makes me  feel that i can achieve anything that i  want  on good days he now makes more than 1  000 euros up to 200 customers find their  way to his home in the soweto township  and almost everyone here heard about the  place online  this morning smiling  i got it on facebook on social media on  tiktok instagram as well on facebook i  found it on social media and when i  found out about it i was like wow  that's he's awesome he's really cool for  doing such things about with a little  amount of money it's very cool most of  our  marketing 